<title>MEXICO: Mexico crude port reopen as wind speeds decline.</title>
<headline>Mexico crude port reopen as wind speeds decline.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico crude ports Pajaritos in Veracruz state and Dos Bocas in Tabasco state reopened at 0630 local/1230 GMT Tuesday as wind speeds in the region relaxed, port officials told Reuters.</p>
<p>The ports shut to crude shipping Sunday at between 1530 and 1600 local as wind speeds reached 45 km per hour and waves were nine feet high.</p>
</text>
